WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.850
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.162
which takes about sixty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:09.469
You'll say why an access key, an
API key, an auth token or a customer

4
00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:14.412
secret key is a long-lived secret, and
what the program does with each one.

5
00:00:14.412 --> 00:00:17.149
You'll name what the
guide's export steps read,

6
00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:20.625
and what AWS's credential report
and list calls leave out.

7
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:23.687
You'll join an identity to
its record with four tags.

8
00:00:23.687 --> 00:00:27.800
You'll run Chapter 13's checks on
fixtures and read what they find.

9
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.713
And you'll name what's still unknown,
and why the kit doesn't assume an answer.

10
00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:34.799
Before you start, finish Modules 1 and 4.

11
00:00:34.799 --> 00:00:38.734
You need PowerShell 7.1
or later with Pester 5,

12
00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:42.790
and no AWS account, O C I
tenancy or Entra tenant.
